STATUS     := PROPOSED (Claude PROPOSE; Devon DECIDE / PROMOTE; Codex binds into mal-fabric on Devon's word)
DATE       := 2026-10-24 America/New_York
KIND       := vocabulary erratum (E-series). Adds NO law. Names what promoted law already states; forbids a folk substitution.
              This file is an erratum, NOT a specification: SPEC-MAL-SPECIFICATION-SYSTEM-002 CHECK_FORM W1–W8 applies to
              specifications and is NOT claimed, exempted or altered here. W9 (below) is an ADDITIONAL check for PROMOTE.
ORIGIN     := Devon 2026-10-24 15:59 "'Hydrogen' is a shape"; 16:03 "'Atom' needs to go as well. What we have is an admissibility
              lattice where the first shape defines the admissible tessellations."

RETIRES (as LAW-POSITION tokens; see W9 for the definition of law position)
  "atom"      — stoichiometry-prototype lattice term (platonic_stoichiometry.jsx AAF00A72…: minimal element of B(≤3)).
                Folk load: a smallest constituent prior to admissibility. The construction has none.
  "hydrogen"  — physical-element name. Admissible ONLY as a correspondence label (physical-element correspondence is the law's
                own MAYBE: SPEC_QUEUEGATE_CONSTRUCTED_UNIVERSE_GENESIS_001 v0.1.0 8A9986EB…42252C, §24 O_next).
  Already retired in principles, same status: "particle", "element" (as entity primitive), "singularity", "entropy", "tie".
  (The words above are MENTIONED here, not USED; W9 distinguishes the two.)

STATES (the construction's own words; forcing clauses cited by document)
  ADMISSIBILITY LATTICE  := the Governed Reaction Lattice over carrier configurations — Governed_Reaction_Lattice.docx
                            83B5E5F0AD3EF5762777787071C1FB78617AB1952900459B01F4666EE46A5A4B: §3 C_M dependent pair
                            (configuration := (arrangement, admissibility witness), :113–119); §4 A_M. Membership = admissibility.
                            Not composition.
  TYPED CHAIN            := F3 fold-receipt 563F99BA…3D93 returns the TYPE basis {Tetrahedron, Cube, Octahedron, Dodecahedron,
                            Icosahedron} (SELF_UNFOLDING_ELEMENT_BASIS_V1 FF0319B1… :97/:203) →
                            basis TYPES vs ElementInstances: QUEUEGATE 8A9986EB… §9 :216–225; multiplicity M : E → Nat §11 :261 →
                            the configured instance (D,I), multiplicity 1 each, over the type basis →
                            ProjectionShell (2,0) by A9/B3 → carrier 012 82E388FD…15BDB (RECTIFICATION_OF_DODECAHEDRAL_ICOSAHEDRAL_DUAL_PAIR).
  THE FIRST SHAPE        := the configured (D,I) @ (2,0) at the end of that chain: the first fold's product.
  WHAT IT DOES           := defines the admissible tessellations. Genealogical constraint on EVERY step: G_parts,n+1 = G_whole,n+1
                            (QUEUEGATE §§6–7). Multiset preservation on HORIZONTAL folds: GRL §4 (a fold is horizontal);
                            VERTICAL steps (refinement) are governed by GRL §7 and require K — not asserted preserved here.
                            MULTISET_PRESERVED terminal in SPEC-J17-WORLD-FOLD-EFFECT-001 E2A87BDC… is the horizontal case.
  ADMISSIBLE TESSELLATIONS := the ProjectionShell(m,n) refinements of the first shape: the 12 domains inherited on the 12
                            directions at every (m,n); the hexagon field between them grows (10T − 10); closure by the twelve
                            pentagonal defects (the dual pair is where the hexagon field — the tiled circle — is forced to close).
                            TRACE_RESONANCE_THROUGH_DERIVED_SHAPES_001 (2026-10-25) §§3–5; The_Projection_Shell.docx.
  REGISTRY (Devon R1, 2026-10-25): ONE primitive shape, the inverted triangle. rectangle := two triangles on a shared edge;
                            circle := the closed fan of six triads around G. The first shape is DERIVED from the primitive, not a
                            second primitive. "Three primitive shapes" retired as scaffold.
  "base shape"           := the above. Not "smallest". Not "building block".
  RETAINED (not retired by "no pieces"): incidence (flag := (site, edge, triad); 720 overlaps); multiplicity (M : E → Nat);
                            G_parts / G_whole as GENEALOGICAL roles under the fold (§§6–7). "No pieces" := no constituent prior to
                            admissibility; parts exist as genealogical roles with multiplicities, not as building blocks.

WRITING RULE
  shape first, label bracketed:   the first shape (D,I) @ (2,0) ["hydrogen", correspondence MAYBE]
  Labels never appear bare in a law position. Prose, comments and string literals may use them.

W9 — RETIRED-TOKEN LAW-POSITION CHECK (additional PROMOTE check; operates on PARSED positions, not on a word search)
  LAW POSITION := any of: identifier declared by `law <id> :=`; `domain <id>`; `@propose seed <id>`; an argument of an operator
                  application inside a law body (THIS(...), GOES_WITH(...), IF ... THEN ...); an `@readonly input` name;
                  a member of a TERMINAL enumeration; a type or kind name in a CONTACTS/OPERANDS binding.
  MENTION      := inside a `//` comment; inside a string literal "..."; inside a RETIRES list of an erratum; inside a
                  bracketed correspondence `[ "<label>", correspondence MAYBE ]` following a shape term; inside a
                  backtick-quoted VECTOR SPECIMEN in the VECTORS section of an erratum or spec (the standalone fixture file
                  carrying the same bytes IS subject to W9; its embedded quotation is not).
  W9(file)     := NO  IF_THEN some retired token occurs in a LAW POSITION;  IF_THEN otherwise.
  RETIRED      := { atom, hydrogen, particle, element, singularity, entropy, tie }  (case-insensitive on the token; whole token).

VECTORS (input bytes frozen in this file; W9 only; expected = sorted-key compact JSON, no terminal newline, uppercase digests)
